# Local AI/development-agent instruction files are generated or machine-facing
# development scaffolding, not part of the public project surface.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Gate 4B: the rendered staging admission-service config carries a real
# staging public-key value and must never be committed. Only this exact
# filename is ignored; deployment/admission-service.staging.template.jsonc
# (the placeholder template) stays tracked.
deployment/admission-service.staging.jsonc

# Gate 5A: the three reviewed rendered Gate 5 staging configs carry real
# account/public-key values and must never be committed. Only these exact
# filenames are ignored; their .template.jsonc sources stay tracked. This is
# a hygiene backstop only -- the primary safety boundary is the exact-filename
# invariant enforced by the preflight/deploy tooling itself, not this glob.
deployment/operator-lifecycle-executor.staging.jsonc
deployment/lifecycle-mailbox.staging.jsonc
deployment/lifecycle-observer.staging.jsonc

# Gate 6A: the rendered staging lifecycle-transport manifest carries a real
# accountId and staging environment identity (no secret access key) and must
# never be committed. Only this exact filename is ignored;
# deployment/lifecycle-transport.staging.template.json (the placeholder
# template) stays tracked. This is a hygiene backstop only -- the primary
# safety boundary is the exact-filename invariant enforced by the staging
# preflight/submit tooling itself, not this glob. Gate 6 local R2 credential
# capture files (accessKeyId/secretAccessKey) are never written under this
# repository at all -- scripts/gate6-credential-capture.ts refuses any
# repo-contained output path outright, so no glob for them is needed here.
deployment/lifecycle-transport.staging.json
